  <main id="main">

    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="page-head industry-head">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Solutions</span>
        <h1>Start with the problem. <em>We&rsquo;ll find the practical fix.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Sometimes the answer is a better website. Sometimes it&rsquo;s a simple automation, a dashboard, or an AI tool. Here are the kinds of problems we solve, and the tools that fit each one.</p>
        <div class="btn-row page-head__cta">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary btn--large" data-review-open data-track="cta-solutions-tell">Tell us what&rsquo;s slowing you down</button>
          <a href="ai-demos" class="btn btn--ghost btn--large" data-track="cta-solutions-examples">See examples</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TYPES ============ -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="types" aria-labelledby="typesTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Five kinds of solution</span>
          <h2 id="typesTitle">Which one fits depends on the problem.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="types reveal">
          <li><a href="services#websites"><b>Websites and online enquiries</b><span>When customers can&rsquo;t find you, or can&rsquo;t easily get in touch.</span><em>from R1,000</em></a></li>
          <li><a href="#library"><b>Workflow automation</b><span>When the same task is done by hand every day or week.</span><em>from R2,000</em></a></li>
          <li><a href="services#dashboards"><b>Dashboards and reporting</b><span>When the numbers are scattered and nobody sees the whole picture.</span><em>from R2,000</em></a></li>
          <li><a href="#knowledge"><b>AI assistants and knowledge tools</b><span>When the same questions get answered, or searched for, over and over.</span><em>from R3,500</em></a></li>
          <li><a href="services#software"><b>Custom software and integrations</b><span>When off-the-shelf tools don&rsquo;t fit how you work, or don&rsquo;t talk to each other.</span><em>from R4,500</em></a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted reveal" style="margin-top:1rem">Not sure which? That&rsquo;s normal. <button type="button" class="inline-link" data-review-open>Describe the problem</button> and we&rsquo;ll suggest the simplest thing that works.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ LIBRARY ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="library" aria-labelledby="libTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Problems we solve · automate repetitive work</span>
          <h2 id="libTitle">The work that arrives, gets read, and gets typed up.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sol-grid sol-grid--4">
          <article class="sol reveal" id="enquiries"><h3>Enquiry handling</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Reading emails and web forms, working out what the person needs, looking up prices and rules, writing the reply.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Reads each enquiry, extracts the requirements, checks your knowledge base and prepares the reply for a person to approve. Routes the unusual ones.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Minutes to prepare a reply · time to first response · share sent without edits</dd></dl><a class="sol__try" href="ai-demos#calls">Try the demo →</a></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="quotes"><h3>Quotes &amp; proposals</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Copying details from an enquiry into a quote template, pricing it line by line, writing the cover note.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Builds the draft quote from the enquiry and your price rules, with the reasoning shown, ready to check and send.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Minutes per quote · quotes sent per day · time from enquiry to quote</dd></dl></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="documents"><h3>Invoice &amp; document capture</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Opening attachments and retyping supplier invoices, orders, forms and statements into your systems.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Reads the document, extracts the fields, checks them against your records and posts them, flagging anything that doesn&rsquo;t match.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Minutes per document · error rate · exceptions caught</dd></dl></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="triage"><h3>Email triage</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>A shared inbox someone has to sort every morning: who should handle what, and what&rsquo;s urgent.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Classifies each message, summarises it, assigns it to the right person or queue and highlights the urgent ones.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Hours a week sorting · time to the right person · missed urgent items</dd></dl></article>
        </div>

        <div class="section__head reveal" style="margin-top:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,4rem)">
          <span class="eyebrow">Connect your existing software</span>
          <h2>The work that exists because your systems don&rsquo;t talk.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sol-grid">
          <article class="sol reveal" id="data-entry"><h3>Data entry between systems</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Keying the same customer, job or order into the CRM, the job system and the accounting package.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Moves the data between your systems as it changes, cleans it on the way, and tells someone when a record doesn&rsquo;t fit.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Hours a week re-keying · mismatches between systems</dd></dl></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="onboarding"><h3>Client onboarding</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Chasing forms and documents, checking they&rsquo;re complete, setting the client up in each system.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Collects the documents, checks them against your checklist, asks for what&rsquo;s missing and creates the client everywhere it needs to exist.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Days to onboard · staff minutes per client · incomplete files</dd></dl></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="reporting"><h3>Monthly reporting</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Exporting from three systems into a spreadsheet, building the same charts, writing the same commentary.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Pulls the numbers on schedule, builds the report and drafts the commentary on what changed, for a person to finalise.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Hours per report · days after month-end it&rsquo;s ready</dd></dl><a class="sol__try" href="ai-demos#insight">Try the demo →</a></article>
        </div>

        <div class="section__head reveal" style="margin-top:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,4rem)">
          <span class="eyebrow">Better access to information</span>
          <h2>The answers your team already has, if only they could find them.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sol-grid">
          <article class="sol reveal" id="knowledge"><h3>Staff knowledge base</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Searching shared drives, PDFs and old emails for a policy, price or procedure &mdash; or interrupting the person who knows.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Turns the documents your staff search manually into one integrated knowledge base. Ask in plain language; get the answer with its source linked.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Minutes to find an answer · questions to senior staff</dd></dl><a class="sol__try" href="ai-demos#rag">Try the demo →</a></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="customer-answers"><h3>Customer questions</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Answering the same questions about hours, prices, availability and process on WhatsApp, chat and email.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Answers from your real information, day and night, captures the details of real leads and hands them to your team.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Questions answered without staff · after-hours leads captured · response time</dd></dl><a class="sol__try" href="ai-demos#qa">Try the demo →</a></article>
          <article class="sol reveal" id="compliance"><h3>Contract &amp; compliance checks</h3>
            <dl><dt>The work</dt><dd>Reading long documents to find the clauses, dates and obligations that matter, and checking nothing&rsquo;s missing.</dd>
            <dt>The system</dt><dd>Extracts the key terms, compares them with your standard and flags gaps and deadlines for a person to review.</dd>
            <dt>We measure</dt><dd>Minutes per review · issues caught before signing</dd></dl></article>
        </div>
        <p class="psr-note reveal">Not on the list? Most of what we build starts as &ldquo;we spend too long on&hellip;&rdquo;. Bring that sentence to a process review.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WHO ============ -->
    <section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="fitTitle">
      <div class="container band">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Where it fits best</span>
          <h2 id="fitTitle">Teams of 5 to 200 that run on email, documents and more than one system.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Law and accounting firms, property and estate agencies, brokers, medical and dental practices, logistics and distribution, trades and field services &mdash; anywhere skilled people spend hours on work a system could prepare for them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ UNDER THE HOOD ============ -->
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="hoodTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Under the hood</span>
          <h2 id="hoodTitle">You buy the outcome. We choose the parts.</h2>
          <p>The model is one component, and the one most likely to change. We build so it can be swapped without rebuilding your system.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="hood reveal">
          <li><b>Document understanding</b><span>Reading emails, PDFs, scans and forms and pulling out what matters.</span></li>
          <li><b>Search over your own documents</b><span>Answers grounded in your files, with the source shown.</span></li>
          <li><b>Workflow automation</b><span>Multi-step processes that run on their own and hand off to people at the right point.</span></li>
          <li><b>Integrations</b><span>Email, WhatsApp, spreadsheets, CRMs, accounting and job systems, through their APIs.</span></li>
          <li><b>People in the loop</b><span>Approvals wherever a mistake would cost you.</span></li>
          <li><b>Evaluation &amp; monitoring</b><span>Test sets, accuracy checks, usage and cost tracking, every month.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TRY THE REAL ASSISTANT ============ -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="try" aria-labelledby="tryTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">One you can try now</span>
          <h2 id="tryTitle">Ask our own assistant.</h2>
          <p>A customer-questions system running on our site, answering from our own pricing and method. Try to catch it out.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <div class="asst" data-assistant>
            <div class="asst__log" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Conversation">
              <div class="asst__msg asst__msg--ai">Hi! I'm Re-Charge's own AI assistant. Ask me about how Re-Charge works, what it costs, or how results are measured.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="asst__chips">
              <button type="button">What happens in discovery?</button>
              <button type="button">What does Operations include?</button>
              <button type="button">How do you measure ROI?</button>
              <button type="button">Do you still build websites?</button>
            </div>
            <form class="asst__form">
              <label class="sr-only" for="asstIn1">Ask a question</label>
              <input class="asst__input" id="asstIn1" type="text" maxlength="500" placeholder="Ask about the method, pricing or results…" autocomplete="off" />
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary asst__send">Ask</button>
            </form>
            <p class="asst__note">This is real AI, answering from Re-Charge's own information — not a script. It can be wrong; for anything important, check with us on WhatsApp.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Questions</span><h2 id="faqTitle">Straight answers.</h2></div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Do we need to change the software we use?</summary><p>Usually not. We connect to what you already run. If a system has no way in, we&rsquo;ll tell you in discovery and suggest the least disruptive option.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Will it replace our staff?</summary><p>It replaces the repetitive part of their work, not their judgement. Most clients use the hours back for the work they hired those people to do. Adoption is one of the six things we score, because a system nobody uses saves nothing.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What if the AI gets something wrong?</summary><p>We design for it. Where a mistake would cost you, the system prepares and a person approves. We test accuracy before go-live and keep testing it every month in Operations.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Is our data safe?</summary><p>Your data stays in accounts you own, is used only to run your system, and is handled under POPIA. We tell you which providers process it and where, before anything is built.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p>A focused, fixed-scope tool starts from R2,000 for an automation or R3,500 for an AI solution. Automating a whole process across your software is done in stages: a R7,500 discovery (credited if you go ahead), a proof of concept from R18,500 and production from R45,000, with support from R4,500 a month. You get a fixed proposal before anything is built. <a class="inline-link" href="pricing">Full pricing</a></p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CTA ============ -->
    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="ctaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <span class="cta__services">Automate · Connect · Find · Measure</span>
        <h2 id="ctaTitle">Bring one process that takes too long.</h2>
        <p>A free 30-minute review. We&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether AI is the answer.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--light btn--large" data-review-open>Tell us what&rsquo;s slowing you down</button>
          <a href="method" class="btn btn--ghost-light btn--large">See the method</a>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" data-contact-block hidden>Prefer to talk first? <a class="inline-link" href="#" data-contact="whatsapp" hidden>WhatsApp us</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
